WEBVTT

00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:12.090
Alright.

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:18.720
Hi!

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:22.500
Ready for another day of hard work?

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:25.580
This definitely counts as stalking.

00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:28.940
First rule of being a good Badryman!

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:32.100
The pointlessness is the point.

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:33.900
Where do the stairs come in?

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:36.600
Working in Sales is all about the legwork.

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:38.220
Ready or not, here I come!

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:42.360
Wait…

00:00:44.660 --> 00:00:46.040
That's cheating, Shiratori!

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:48.520
I'm not wasting my energy.

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:53.380
[Deep-fried Skewers Pub]
Thank you for your business,
we're from Sunlight Beverage.

00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:56.460
Oh, Miyazumi, perfect timing!

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:59.940
Could I order three extra cases
of Besshonuma Cider?

00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:02.420
Of course! We appreciate your patronage!

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:05.180
I'll have them delivered before the evening.

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:07.180
Love how fast you always work!

00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:08.600
Oh, it's nothing.

00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:10.460
What about the order form?

00:01:10.590 --> 00:01:12.500
Oh, I'll take care of that.

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:14.440
But the manual says…

00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:17.880
Yeah, real life doesn't follow manuals.

00:01:18.040 --> 00:01:20.520
Then what's the point
of having a manual at all?

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:24.240
Second rule of being a good Badryman!

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:25.300
Actually, never mind.

00:02:56.930 --> 00:02:58.200
[#02: Synergy]

00:02:58.200 --> 00:02:59.320
[#02: Synergy]
Warmup over!

00:02:59.320 --> 00:02:59.780
[#02: Synergy]

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:00.960
Basic shots!

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:02.100
Yes, sir!

00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:11.660
Not again… Don't you think
the ceiling's a little low?

00:03:11.660 --> 00:03:13.060
You'll get used to it!

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:15.540
Knocking practice!

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:23.870
Won't we use cameras to check our form?

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:25.300
How? We've got none.

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:28.420
Workout!

00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:35.140
Ten more seconds, hang in there!

00:03:35.380 --> 00:03:36.960
No training equipment?

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:38.740
We're doing fine without it.

00:03:38.740 --> 00:03:43.100
Hey, newbie! How about you stop comparing
our training regimen with Mitsuhoshi's?!

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:45.740
You don't need to be Mitsuhoshi to have standards!

00:03:45.740 --> 00:03:47.520
Shiratori, Tatsu!

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:52.190
Our practice game with Unisics
is coming up this weekend,

00:03:52.190 --> 00:03:54.780
so let's see how well you cooperate!

00:03:54.860 --> 00:03:55.320
Yes, sir.

00:03:56.480 --> 00:03:58.320
Don't you need a racket, Coach?

00:03:58.320 --> 00:03:59.120
Here he comes!

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:02.980
Dude…

00:04:03.280 --> 00:04:04.560
Think fast!

00:04:09.890 --> 00:04:11.940
Ever heard of calling?

00:04:11.940 --> 00:04:13.860
You're not on your own anymore!

00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:25.100
My bad, I should've called it.

00:04:27.040 --> 00:04:28.640
Hey, you okay?

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:31.720
Oh, I'm… fine.

00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:41.780
[Isuzu Diner]
Eight draft beers, one ginger ale please!

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:47.020
Honestly, I didn't think it was possible
to be that out of sync with someone.

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:49.720
How much more are you gonna add?
What's wrong with you?

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:56.420
"We'll make great partners," he said,
and then made no effort to match my pace.

00:04:56.600 --> 00:05:00.140
Hey, I'm not the one
trying to cover the whole court alone.

00:05:02.520 --> 00:05:06.520
Only because you jump all over the place
trying to hit smash shots all the damn time!

00:05:06.560 --> 00:05:09.940
- But jumping smashes are so cool!
- At this rate, we'll universally
get our asses kicked by Uni…

00:05:09.940 --> 00:05:10.940
- I've partnered with a child…
- At this rate, we'll universally
get our asses kicked by Uni…

00:05:11.540 --> 00:05:13.680
Here are your Fukaya scallions.

00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:15.880
Yum!

00:05:15.880 --> 00:05:20.460
Today, we're covering the world's second best
men's badminton player, Kirishima Hayato!

00:05:20.460 --> 00:05:23.140
- Currently playing for Unisics…
- Speak of the devil… That's Hayato, alright.

00:05:23.140 --> 00:05:26.340
- Currently playing for Unisics…
- Oh, right, you mentioned
you went to high school together?

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:29.660
- Known for his looks and playstyle…
- Being hot doesn't make you a better player!

00:05:29.660 --> 00:05:31.660
Just say you're envious and go.

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:37.880
Kirishima, who also works as a model,
will be releasing his first photo book next month!

00:05:38.980 --> 00:05:41.940
- Who does he think he is?!
- Boo, he's not even that hot!

00:05:42.500 --> 00:05:47.150
Can you tell us how you feel about
your younger brother, Kirishima Takuma,

00:05:47.150 --> 00:05:50.360
being the world's best badminton player?

00:05:50.660 --> 00:05:51.900
Takuma is…

00:05:52.360 --> 00:05:56.660
I'd hate it if my younger brother was
the best player in the world.

00:05:56.960 --> 00:05:58.380
I'm right here, you know?

00:05:59.660 --> 00:06:03.840
Let me be clear. If we lose our next game,
it'll be because of you.

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:06.760
Oh, you're already making up excuses
for when we lose?

00:06:06.760 --> 00:06:07.900
Like hell I am!

00:06:08.020 --> 00:06:09.970
If this were a sports anime,

00:06:09.970 --> 00:06:13.300
the reluctant partners fighting
would end with them winning the game.

00:06:13.300 --> 00:06:14.480
Man, I wish.

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:21.780
Waoko is the largest supermarket company
in the prefecture, and my best client by far.

00:06:23.160 --> 00:06:24.740
Looks expensive.

00:06:25.060 --> 00:06:27.740
It's the president's. He loves cars.

00:06:27.990 --> 00:06:28.990
Really…

00:06:30.800 --> 00:06:33.560
[President's office]
Miyazumi! Thanks to your last campaign,

00:06:33.560 --> 00:06:37.620
we've increased our profits by 8%!
That's exactly why we love to work with you.

00:06:37.640 --> 00:06:39.060
Thank you for your patronage.

00:06:39.300 --> 00:06:42.500
I'll have a new proposal ready
the next time I'm here.

00:06:42.840 --> 00:06:44.000
Oh, I can't wait!

00:06:46.700 --> 00:06:49.860
Are we seriously expected to do this in Sales?

00:06:50.140 --> 00:06:52.740
It might seem like a waste of time to you,

00:06:52.740 --> 00:06:55.900
but it's the little things that
eventually create something big.

00:06:56.380 --> 00:06:59.820
Once upon a time, we only got
one row on this shelf for our products.

00:07:00.680 --> 00:07:03.640
Well, don't just stand there.

00:07:03.640 --> 00:07:06.340
Fetch me the FoldCons
and a set of pop from the car.

00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:16.220
Foldable Container, hence FoldCon…

00:07:16.720 --> 00:07:19.260
What am I supposed to
do with this information…

00:07:32.240 --> 00:07:33.720
Our deepest apologies!

00:07:35.480 --> 00:07:39.420
I think you can stop now.
You're bothering the customers.

00:07:39.420 --> 00:07:40.860
Sir, please…

00:07:41.120 --> 00:07:44.340
We've worked with
Sunlight Beverage for years now,

00:07:44.340 --> 00:07:46.860
but perhaps it's time to
rethink this partnership…

00:07:47.680 --> 00:07:50.510
This happened due to my lack of supervision.

00:07:50.810 --> 00:07:53.900
I'll take responsibility for
everything, so please…!

00:07:53.900 --> 00:07:59.080
It took me six months to convince my wife,
and just when I finally got my hands on it…!

00:08:01.940 --> 00:08:03.120
Uh, Shiratori?

00:08:06.800 --> 00:08:07.700
Can I have a word?

00:08:08.200 --> 00:08:09.240
Let go!

00:08:11.300 --> 00:08:12.500
Left hook to my face…

00:08:16.640 --> 00:08:17.840
Crap!

00:08:18.020 --> 00:08:19.080
I knew it!

00:08:19.500 --> 00:08:20.600
You brat…!

00:08:30.800 --> 00:08:31.580
Stay down!

00:08:32.660 --> 00:08:35.340
You can't just run off like that.

00:08:35.620 --> 00:08:37.960
What do you think I'm here for?

00:08:41.100 --> 00:08:42.240
Nice work today!

00:08:46.340 --> 00:08:50.220
The president forgave us,
so all's well that ends well!

00:08:50.720 --> 00:08:52.640
Is that a reason to invite me for drinks?

00:08:52.980 --> 00:08:56.330
How did you know that guy was shoplifting?

00:08:58.260 --> 00:09:00.900
Won't hurt you to tell me, will it?

00:09:04.950 --> 00:09:06.580
Hey, what's that for?

00:09:06.580 --> 00:09:08.660
I'm showing you how it works.

00:09:10.040 --> 00:09:13.750
My Foresight lets me predict
what someone will do

00:09:13.750 --> 00:09:15.720
based on their subconscious movements.

00:09:16.380 --> 00:09:20.240
Put simply, it's a little like
being able to tell the future.

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:25.330
I think everyone tries to predict
how their opponent will move.

00:09:25.330 --> 00:09:27.760
Are you really that special?

00:09:27.860 --> 00:09:32.040
I am. I've been observing people
since I was a kid.

00:09:34.040 --> 00:09:37.560
The power of non-verbal communication, huh…

00:09:37.730 --> 00:09:39.800
Hm? Non-verbal?

00:09:40.320 --> 00:09:43.240
90% of human communication is non-verbal.

00:09:43.240 --> 00:09:48.180
Meaning, communicating by means other than words.

00:09:49.520 --> 00:09:50.740
That's news to me.

00:09:51.040 --> 00:09:52.920
You really are something else!

00:09:53.240 --> 00:09:57.600
I assumed you were all talk, but it looks like
I got myself a real good partner.

00:09:57.600 --> 00:10:01.740
Now, listen. You and I will be a thing
for a limited time only.

00:10:03.700 --> 00:10:07.000
No, you listen. I want to play doubles with you.

00:10:08.500 --> 00:10:11.220
I know! Why don't you give this a shot?

00:10:12.220 --> 00:10:15.320
A new product proposal competition…?

00:10:15.840 --> 00:10:20.680
I don't really care for proposing new products.
Honestly, I'm not even good at sales…

00:10:20.680 --> 00:10:26.180
First rule of being a good Badryman!
The pointlessness is the point!

00:10:26.180 --> 00:10:28.520
Why are drunk people so loud…

00:10:31.840 --> 00:10:35.640
[Unisics Headquarters]

00:10:36.860 --> 00:10:37.580
Whoa…

00:10:49.900 --> 00:10:51.600
A-A-Are you kidding me…?

00:10:51.880 --> 00:10:54.300
T-Talk about an away game…

00:10:54.300 --> 00:10:57.400
In their eyes, we're garnish at best.

00:10:57.780 --> 00:10:59.660
I like eating the garnish, personally.

00:11:00.140 --> 00:11:01.250
Let's talk more later!

00:11:01.900 --> 00:11:02.920
Good morning, sir.

00:11:03.760 --> 00:11:05.680
Miyazumi, long time no see!

00:11:05.800 --> 00:11:06.920
Good to see you again.

00:11:07.400 --> 00:11:09.360
That sure is a lot of cameras!

00:11:09.700 --> 00:11:13.200
[Kirishima Hayato, 25, Unisics]
We'll be announcing a new product today, you see.

00:11:13.500 --> 00:11:16.040
Good to see you, Sota. Glad you're feeling well.

00:11:16.390 --> 00:11:17.100
Thanks.

00:11:17.260 --> 00:11:20.760
'Scuse me, coming through!
You're Miyazumi, right?

00:11:20.880 --> 00:11:26.040
I joined Unisics this year.
Misora Ayato, age 17!

00:11:27.080 --> 00:11:29.900
Could we take a photo together?

00:11:30.240 --> 00:11:31.040
S-Sure.

00:11:31.900 --> 00:11:35.260
I have 500,000 followers on Inste, you know.

00:11:36.700 --> 00:11:38.100
He's already posted it.

00:11:38.340 --> 00:11:39.160
- Show me.
- Lemme see.

00:11:39.200 --> 00:11:41.280
[Meet Tatsu, the old dog of badminton!]

00:11:42.480 --> 00:11:44.620
He called him an "old dog"…!

00:11:44.840 --> 00:11:49.080
In any case, let's have a good game.
I mean, we'll win, but…

00:11:49.080 --> 00:11:49.560
Ow!

00:11:50.140 --> 00:11:51.900
[Oginome Daiki, 25, Unisics]
Are you up to no good again?

00:11:51.900 --> 00:11:53.480
[Oginome Daiki, 25, Unisics]
I was just saying hello!

00:11:53.480 --> 00:11:55.200
Daiki, why so mean?

00:11:55.200 --> 00:11:56.760
Stop riling people up!

00:11:57.780 --> 00:11:59.560
I apologize for them.

00:12:01.600 --> 00:12:04.940
Sorry for the rowdy boys.
Hope to have a good game today.

00:12:05.900 --> 00:12:09.760
We'll blow a hole right through them.
Best be ready.

00:12:10.440 --> 00:12:11.920
Glad to see you never change.

00:12:12.200 --> 00:12:15.280
[Yagami Jun & Natsuki Ryo vs.
Takeda Koki & Saeki Toya]

00:12:17.500 --> 00:12:20.380
T-They're all pumpkins.
Pumpkins. Remember, pumpkins.

00:12:20.520 --> 00:12:21.780
- Bit early for Halloween…
- Pumpkins. Remember, pumpkins.

00:12:23.040 --> 00:12:26.400
Can we stream our game on our channel?

00:12:26.400 --> 00:12:27.920
Absolutely not!

00:12:27.920 --> 00:12:29.200
Naww!

00:12:29.520 --> 00:12:31.200
Not a fan of that attitude.

00:12:31.200 --> 00:12:33.560
They really think we won't put up a fight.

00:12:33.860 --> 00:12:35.400
Love-all. Play!

00:12:43.840 --> 00:12:47.180
Huh. Guess they're
stronger than I thought.

00:12:53.840 --> 00:12:56.480
First game won by Unisics.

00:12:56.800 --> 00:12:58.440
They really are good.

00:12:58.840 --> 00:13:01.360
Yeah… Let's go.

00:13:01.540 --> 00:13:02.260
Let's.

00:13:10.320 --> 00:13:12.560
Ko, relax! We'll get the next one!

00:13:20.100 --> 00:13:21.380
Goddamn it!

00:13:21.740 --> 00:13:24.880
I don't know what their deal is,
but I doubt they'll keep up with us.

00:13:24.880 --> 00:13:26.420
Good for us!

00:13:31.180 --> 00:13:35.360
Game. Match won by Yagami and Natsuki, Unisics.

00:13:36.360 --> 00:13:37.280
Sorry…

00:13:37.280 --> 00:13:39.820
Hey, our team hasn't lost yet.

00:13:39.820 --> 00:13:41.540
But we did!

00:13:42.040 --> 00:13:44.800
[2nd game]
[Saeki Sota vs. Yokosuka Kei]

00:13:46.300 --> 00:13:48.720
First game won by Saeki Sota.

00:13:48.840 --> 00:13:50.380
Get 'em, Sota!

00:13:50.380 --> 00:13:52.140
We're winning in singles!

00:13:56.820 --> 00:14:00.020
I mean, he's strong and all,
but boring as heck.

00:14:00.020 --> 00:14:01.380
They'll hear you!

00:14:01.780 --> 00:14:06.060
Game. Match won by Saeki Sota
from Sunlight Beverage.

00:14:07.400 --> 00:14:09.760
Man, I wish I could play today…

00:14:10.140 --> 00:14:13.980
You're our secret weapon.
You're sitting out until the tournament.

00:14:14.280 --> 00:14:15.820
Oh, I know, I know.

00:14:16.440 --> 00:14:19.920
[3rd game]
[Miyazumi Tatsuru & Shiratori Mikoto vs.
Kirishima Hayato & Oginome Daiki]

00:14:20.300 --> 00:14:23.720
One on one, huh? That's better than I thought.

00:14:24.120 --> 00:14:26.290
I thought I wouldn't get a chance to…

00:14:27.160 --> 00:14:28.640
You talk too much.

00:14:34.260 --> 00:14:35.600
Love-all. Play!

00:14:38.940 --> 00:14:39.500
He's good!

00:14:43.120 --> 00:14:43.880
Mine!

00:14:48.760 --> 00:14:52.060
Let's go, Hayato!
You're perfect as always!

00:15:02.420 --> 00:15:05.260
We're just getting started.
Too early to panic.

00:15:06.020 --> 00:15:07.080
I know.

00:15:07.320 --> 00:15:08.720
They're pulling ahead.

00:15:08.840 --> 00:15:11.780
He needs time to observe
his opponent to use Foresight, right?

00:15:11.920 --> 00:15:15.340
Usually, yeah, but… I think this is different.

00:15:20.880 --> 00:15:21.940
I can't figure him out!

00:15:22.900 --> 00:15:26.580
He doesn't have the tells most people do.

00:15:27.900 --> 00:15:31.260
Honestly, this vanguard ain't helping either!

00:15:35.120 --> 00:15:35.900
Damn it…

00:16:01.380 --> 00:16:03.580
Mikoto can't use his Foresight…

00:16:03.900 --> 00:16:06.660
And they're aiming at him!

00:16:07.060 --> 00:16:10.260
Between the two of them,
Hayato has a powerful smash shot,

00:16:10.720 --> 00:16:14.480
but Oginome's diligent vanguard
is taking its toll.

00:16:14.660 --> 00:16:18.300
Who thought the world's second-best
player would be so good!

00:16:18.800 --> 00:16:21.620
First game won by Unisics.

00:16:22.160 --> 00:16:24.840
Are you anxious
that our opponents are out of our league?

00:16:25.160 --> 00:16:25.840
Am not.

00:16:26.000 --> 00:16:28.420
Then why's your head not in the game?

00:16:28.640 --> 00:16:29.980
Well, what did you…!

00:16:30.180 --> 00:16:31.660
Finally you've looked at me.

00:16:32.960 --> 00:16:36.440
Seriously. What do you think I'm here for?

00:16:37.960 --> 00:16:41.760
I'll get all the shots you miss.

00:16:44.700 --> 00:16:46.400
Love-all. Play!

00:16:53.000 --> 00:16:53.900
Let me at it!

00:17:13.640 --> 00:17:15.820
Once the shuttlecock falls, you've lost.

00:17:16.240 --> 00:17:19.260
And I don't want to lose. How about you?

00:17:21.120 --> 00:17:22.760
I have an idea.

00:17:33.760 --> 00:17:36.220
Straight? No, cross shot…?

00:17:37.240 --> 00:17:37.980
Cross shot!

00:17:39.780 --> 00:17:40.540
He got it?!

00:17:41.560 --> 00:17:42.480
I can do this!

00:17:49.720 --> 00:17:51.440
- Hell yeah!
- Let's frickin' go!

00:17:57.100 --> 00:17:57.840
No way…

00:18:01.880 --> 00:18:02.660
He figured me out?

00:18:04.980 --> 00:18:05.840
Which way…?

00:18:08.340 --> 00:18:09.160
No…!

00:18:11.240 --> 00:18:12.580
All according to plan!

00:18:13.780 --> 00:18:15.540
I have an idea.

00:18:17.100 --> 00:18:21.840
Even with no clear tells,
I can narrow down the course of his hit.

00:18:22.040 --> 00:18:24.320
From there, I'll make a wager.

00:18:24.740 --> 00:18:26.840
Will that be enough?

00:18:27.040 --> 00:18:30.420
If I get it wrong,
go for it as if your life depends on it.

00:18:30.840 --> 00:18:32.700
Isn't that what you're here for?

00:18:35.470 --> 00:18:38.390
Now that's what I like to hear!

00:18:46.200 --> 00:18:46.780
How…?

00:18:56.600 --> 00:18:58.980
I can see it… This is it.

00:18:59.850 --> 00:19:01.170
This is the feeling…!

00:19:04.800 --> 00:19:05.660
We can do this!

00:19:05.880 --> 00:19:06.440
Yeah!

00:19:08.280 --> 00:19:10.060
You thought it'd be that easy?

00:19:11.520 --> 00:19:12.280
There we go!

00:19:23.280 --> 00:19:25.920
Once the shuttlecock falls, you've lost.

00:19:30.460 --> 00:19:31.760
A cross shot? Really?

00:19:41.960 --> 00:19:45.080
Second game won by Sunlight Beverage.

00:19:45.400 --> 00:19:47.620
- Let's go!
- They turned it around…

00:19:48.240 --> 00:19:52.200
No way… Hayato and Oginome never lose…

00:19:54.560 --> 00:19:58.020
How far ahead can he see…?

00:19:58.180 --> 00:20:01.340
How many years has it been
since we lost a game in a practice match?

00:20:01.820 --> 00:20:03.060
Time to switch it up.

00:20:03.240 --> 00:20:03.860
Okay.

00:20:04.600 --> 00:20:06.080
This might actually be fun.

00:20:08.820 --> 00:20:11.640
Final game. Love-all. Play!

00:20:25.820 --> 00:20:27.900
Are you still sulking?

00:20:28.260 --> 00:20:31.180
Sure, we lost, but it wasn't for nothing.

00:20:31.930 --> 00:20:34.910
In that final game, we got our asses beat.

00:20:35.240 --> 00:20:38.500
And we'll let them know what that feels like
at the Tournament in June.

00:20:38.940 --> 00:20:41.920
Don't forget they're not the only
opponents to look out for.

00:20:42.260 --> 00:20:43.820
We're not losing again.

00:20:44.400 --> 00:20:45.420
Never again!

00:20:46.600 --> 00:20:48.620
Are you extending the limited time offer?

00:20:50.600 --> 00:20:55.380
For now, we're… united against
a common enemy until the Tournament.

00:20:58.200 --> 00:21:00.120
I know we can do this, Mikoto!

00:21:01.060 --> 00:21:02.920
You can use my first name too!

00:21:03.400 --> 00:21:04.740
Uh, I'd rather not.

00:21:05.580 --> 00:21:07.680
Hey, could you tell me…

00:21:08.440 --> 00:21:10.460
What's keeping you from jumping?

00:22:46.020 --> 00:22:47.860
[Tomari Transport]

00:22:47.860 --> 00:22:50.720
Lunch break, everyone!

00:22:56.110 --> 00:22:59.040
[Unisics wins practice game with
Sunlight Beverage 2-1]

00:23:02.860 --> 00:23:04.040
It can't be…

00:23:05.840 --> 00:23:09.720
[Message from Toya:
Mikoto is playing doubles again]

00:23:12.280 --> 00:23:13.420
Mikoto?
